a45d5e66adab19e19a25f157b3f2e40996dce9e6f8adcd7d059a274a67c","event_uuid":"d820d67b-7aac-48ef-a2a3-0e004041ae13","position":{"commit_sha":"85db58d66fea34d4ad6c1bed36d1e4b7114a96a6","position":"1787376833613831332-d820d67b-7aac-48ef-a2a3-0e004041ae13"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"68b6c548bdbb22a4edb98153cf88a3808667d2b1eb1dca5f826580c5f07d279b","event_uuid":"3f5478c5-4aa9-47cb-9b8d-783239cf1cfc","position":{"commit_sha":"4e85182cd693ef49e1435e28f02c9f4d3a9ee5c6","position":"1787381224740300167-3f5478c5-4aa9-47cb-9b8d-783239cf1cfc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787290334619111001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a305bcd3-2cc2-4d94-ac3c-4c1758779cba","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141"},{"link_uuid":"14be54b1-8ba3-4347-84e3-49a23154e97b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dae6-6c92-b127-4aa2"},{"link_uuid":"42faafca-dec2-4a3e-9f78-54c5ec17710d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"34d9-c720-4986-46f8"},{"link_uuid":"d820d67b-7aac-48ef-a2a3-0e004041ae13","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"edf4-ed43-1649-4a61"},{"link_uuid":"3f5478c5-4aa9-47cb-9b8d-783239cf1cfc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5a9b-8958-8a5e-413e"}],"description":"# S8 — `rebar bridge suggest-mapping`: live Jira probe to pre-populate mapping config\n\n## Context / Problem\nEpic 3d7a (S1–S5) adds the mapping seam: a reserved `[mapping]` / `[tool.rebar.mapping]`\nblock with per-layer vocabulary (`statuses`, `issue_types`, `link_types`, `hierarchy`)\nand axis maps (`status_map`, `type_map`, `link_map`, `priority_map`, `create_defaults`),\nparsed by `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mapping_config.py` (S1). Hand-authoring it\nis transcription-error-prone. S8 adds a READ-ONLY command that observes a live Jira\nproject via the pycontribs client and emits a suggested `[tool.rebar.mapping]` block\nseeded with the project's real vocabulary and identity-seed axis maps.\n\nFindings resolved:\n- Verb `rebar bridge probe` COLLIDES with the retired alias `bridge-probe`\n  (`_registry.py:579`; parser `_parsers/advanced/bridge.py:117`; handler `_bridge_probe`\n  `_cli/__init__.py:103`, which CREATES+DELETES a throwaway issue — not read-only). New\n  verb: **`rebar bridge suggest-mapping`** (verified free in `src/`+`tests/`).\n- No private `_get_json` — it exists ONLY on the Gerrit client\n  (`review_bot/gerrit_client.py:128`), not the jira adapter, which uses only HIGH-LEVEL\n  `jira.JIRA` methods; the probe uses only such methods (below).\n- No tomlkit; TOML read via stdlib `tomllib`; `_emit_toml` is fail-closed on nesting, so\n  an orchestrator + dedicated nested emitter are added (below).\n\n## Approach\nNew verb wired into the bridge group (NEW):\n- Parser: `commands.add_parser(\"suggest-mapping\", ...)` in\n  `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/bridge.py` (beside `check-access` ~line 117), taking\n  `<PROJECT>` and `--write`.\n- Dispatch: add `\"suggest-mapping\"` to `bridge_cli`'s pass-through set\n  (`src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py:259`) + a `_passthrough`/`_passthrough_help`\n  branch → NEW handler `_bridge_suggest_mapping` (`_cli/__init__.py`, sibling of\n  `_bridge_probe`).\n\nProbe (NEW `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mapping_probe.py`, <800 LOC): a probe\nPORT with one narrow method per axis, each a thin call to a pycontribs `jira.JIRA`\nmethod. Default port built from `build_client_from_settings`\n(`adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py:155`); tests inject a FAKE port → offline. Pin\n`jira>=3.8,<4` (pyproject.toml:202).\n\nAxis grounding — every axis uses a HIGH-LEVEL method (no private REST):\n- `issue_types` + `hierarchy` → `jira.JIRA.issue_types()` (read each `hierarchyLevel`;\n  if absent, `hierarchy` is DROPPED empty + note, not fabricated).\n- `priority_map` vocab → `jira.JIRA.priorities()`; `link_types` →\n  `jira.JIRA.issue_link_types()` (documented public).\n- `statuses` vocab → `jira.JIRA.statuses()` (documented public). pycontribs exposes no\n  per-PROJECT status list publicly, so this is the GLOBAL set — the block documents that\n  honest limitation.\n- `create_defaults` stubs → `jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes(<KEY>)` +\n  `createmeta_fieldtypes(<KEY>, <id>)` (public createmeta API); stub only for a\n  `required: true` field NOT in the create BASELINE (see AC footer).\n- transition hints (best-effort) → grounded in the ACTUAL transitions surface:\n  `jira.JIRA.search_issues(jql)` (CONFIRMED in DC adapter) fetches one sample issue per\n  discovered type, then `jira.JIRA.transitions(issue)` (CONFIRMED at\n  `adapters/jira_datacenter/transitions.py:80`). Jira returns transitions only from each\n  sample's CURRENT status, so the set is inherently partial → flagged best-effort.\n  `status_map` stays identity-seeded; transition data is an ADVISORY marker, not complete.\n\nAnchor: `search_issues`, `transitions`, `fields` are confirmed in-repo on this same\n`jira.JIRA` client (DC adapter); the vocabulary getters are documented pycontribs 3.x\npublic API.\n\nEmit: build `{\"projects\": {<KEY>: {<layer>}}}`.\n- Default (no `--write`): serialize that block to stdout as TOML. NEVER writes; reads only.\n- `--write`: mirror `write_jira_config`'s target-selection + read-whole/mutate/atomic-\n  replace. Target via `config._discover_project_config` → existing `rebar.toml`, else\n  create `<repo_root>/rebar.toml`; user `pyproject.toml` is NEVER edited. Read with\n  `tomllib`, DEEP-MERGE under `data[\"mapping\"][\"projects\"][<KEY>]` (EXISTING keys win,\n  hand edits never clobbered), re-emit the WHOLE file via the orchestrator below, atomic\n  `os.replace`.\n\nSerialization — OPTION B, a top-level ORCHESTRATOR (a real `rebar.toml` mixes FLAT\nsiblings `[jira]`/`[tracker]` with the NESTED `[mapping.*]`, so no single emitter can\nwrite the whole file). `_config_writer._emit_toml` (:188) fail-closes on any nested\nsub-table — pinned by `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py:149`\n(`_emit_toml({\"jira\": {\"nested\": {\"k\": \"v\"}}})` must raise `ConfigError`); UNTOUCHED. S8\nadds two NEW helpers in `_config_writer.py`:\n- `_emit_nested_toml(name, table)` — recurses one nested table into dotted-header\n  sub-tables (`[mapping.projects.KEY.status_map]`); only ever handed the `mapping` table.\n- `_emit_config_toml(data)` — orchestrator: split off the reserved `mapping` key, emit\n  ALL remaining top-level items (scalars + the flat `[jira]`/`[tracker]` siblings it did\n  NOT author) via the EXISTING `_emit_toml`, then append\n  `_emit_nested_toml(\"mapping\", data[\"mapping\"])` when present, joined by a blank line.\n`_emit_toml` never receives the `mapping` table, so its fail-closed contract + pinned test\nstand; flat siblings round-trip through the flat path, nested `[mapping.*]` through the\nnested path. The `--write` handler calls `_emit_config_toml`; `write_jira_config` keeps\ncalling `_emit_toml` unchanged. HONEST SCOPE: `tomllib` drops comments (no tomlkit), so\nthe merge keeps existing hand-edited VALUES (existing keys win) but inline comments in\n`[mapping]` are NOT preserved.\n\n## Scope\n- NEW `mapping_probe.py` (probe port + per-axis getters + layer builder + TOML emit),\n  <800 LOC.\n- NEW `_config_writer._emit_nested_toml` + `_emit_config_toml` orchestrator (per\n  Serialization); `_emit_toml` (:188) + pinned `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py:149`\n  stay UNTOUCHED.\n- Wire: `bridge.py` parser, `_bridge_commands.py` dispatch, `__init__.py` handler (NEW).\n- Out of scope: WRITE to Jira; live-credential CI gating; comment round-tripping.\n\n## Testing\nTests use a FAKE probe port returning canned issue-type/priority/link-type/status/\ncreatemeta/search+transitions data — fully offline, no live Jira or CI credential\n(portability rule). A live smoke run is manual, never a CI gate. New tests in\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_probe.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `test_probe_emits_mapping` — `rebar bridge suggest-mapping <KEY>` against the fake\n      port emits a `[tool.rebar.mapping]` block with discovered vocabulary (`issue_types`,\n      `statuses`, `link_types`, priorities, `hierarchy` when `hierarchyLevel` present),\n      identity-seed axis maps, and `create_defaults` stubs.\n- [ ] `test_probe_is_read_only` — default invocation writes NO file; the fake port\n      records only reads (no create/transition/delete), distinct from `check-access`.\n- [ ] `test_probe_write_preserves_edits` — `--write` into a `rebar.toml` that already\n      has flat `[jira]`+`[tracker]` sections PRESERVES both AND adds `[mapping.*]`;\n      deep-merge under `projects.<KEY>` keeps a pre-existing hand-edited mapping key\n      (existing keys win); `pyproject.toml` is never edited.\n- [ ] `test_probe_transitions_best_effort` — fake port returns `search_issues` samples +\n      per-issue `transitions()` limited to each sample's current status; emitted\n      transition hints are flagged best-effort/partial (comment/marker), never asserted\n      complete; `status_map` stays identity-seeded.\n\n\"create_defaults\" baseline (concrete): the outbound create path\n`adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158` (`map_local_to_remote`) already supplies\n`summary`, `description`, `issuetype`, `priority`, `assignee`, conditionally `status`+\n`parent`; a stub is emitted ONLY for a createmeta `required: true` field NOT in that\nbaseline.\n\nTest tier: unit","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/probe.py","reason":"new Jira probe module"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/bridge.py","reason":"rebar bridge probe CLI wiring"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_probe.py","reason":"new probe tests against faked REST client"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141"],["parent","3d7a-7795-efde-4df7"],["relates_to","34d9-c720-4986-46f8"],["relates_to","5a9b-8958-8a5e-413e"],["relates_to","dae6-6c92-b127-4aa2"],["relates_to","edf4-ed43-1649-4a61"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","parent_status_uuid":"37570021-3122-4283-a547-77918b8a9c41","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ad81-73ad-83bb-47c7","ticket_type":"story","title":"Live Jira probe command to pre-populate mapping config","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6ed1b044-5fad-4f93-8d62-1ff2fa34f832","7f416eda-a5d5-417e-82f7-d28c4b2c71b9","9929d2f9-e979-4ef2-b917-3a36b633a791","f0183050-e101-4b51-94be-a29a84dd2b7b","6e3e4ef9-f05c-4ff9-b010-71c6797fa667","37570021-3122-4283-a547-77918b8a9c41","2e8d7039-4684-47e7-ad94-9ed28809cd95","14be54b1-8ba3-4347-84e3-49a23154e97b","42faafca-dec2-4a3e-9f78-54c5ec17710d","d820d67b-7aac-48ef-a2a3-0e004041ae13","3f5478c5-4aa9-47cb-9b8d-783239cf1cfc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787384183631752001,"uuid":"0722ff19-7abd-4834-9a7f-1972ab0b5f89"}